CLAIMS

1. A computer-implemented system for AI-powered interpretation of aviation regulatory requirements comprising:
   a) a natural language processing engine that analyzes regulatory text using advanced linguistic algorithms to extract semantic meaning and regulatory intent;
   b) a contextual interpretation module that adapts regulatory interpretations based on operational scenarios and organizational factors;
   c) an ambiguity detection and resolution algorithm that systematically identifies unclear regulatory language and generates resolution recommendations;
   d) a compliance guidance generator that translates regulatory requirements into actionable implementation steps with resource estimates and timelines;
   e) wherein the system provides automated interpretation of complex regulatory language while maintaining accuracy and consistency.

2. The system of claim 1, wherein the natural language processing engine employs domain-specific regulatory parsing algorithms and entity recognition trained on aviation regulatory corpora.

3. The system of claim 1, wherein the contextual interpretation module considers operational type, organizational scale, regulatory environment, and risk profile factors in generating context-aware interpretations.

4. The system of claim 1, wherein the ambiguity detection algorithm classifies ambiguities by type and severity, generating resolution recommendations based on historical interpretations and expert knowledge.

5. The system of claim 1, wherein the compliance guidance generator optimizes implementation sequences considering resource constraints, dependencies, and regulatory timelines.

6. A method for AI-powered interpretation of aviation regulatory requirements comprising:
   a) analyzing regulatory text using natural language processing to extract semantic meaning and identify regulatory concepts;
   b) applying contextual interpretation based on operational scenarios and organizational characteristics;
   c) detecting ambiguities in regulatory language and generating resolution recommendations using machine learning algorithms;
   d) translating interpreted requirements into actionable compliance guidance with implementation procedures and validation criteria;
   e) continuously learning from interpretation outcomes to improve accuracy and consistency.

7. The method of claim 6, wherein analyzing regulatory text includes syntactic parsing, semantic role identification, and regulatory concept extraction using domain-specific knowledge bases.

8. The method of claim 6, wherein contextual interpretation includes assessment of organizational capabilities, resource constraints, and implementation capacity.

9. The method of claim 6, wherein ambiguity detection includes linguistic, semantic, and pragmatic ambiguity classification with severity assessment and expert review integration.

10. The method of claim 6, wherein compliance guidance generation includes implementation optimization, risk mitigation planning, and validation protocol establishment.

11. The system of claim 1, further comprising a machine learning training system that continuously refines interpretation models based on expert feedback and implementation outcomes.

12. The method of claim 6, further comprising quality assurance validation through expert review workflows and confidence scoring for interpretation accuracy.

